:: Internship Overview Meetings [event sister_quest scene] {"position":"3275,1325","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "Internship Overview Meetings" (sister_internshipOverviewRequest), part 1 of 2. A couple of days after
   It Makes A Difference: she brings the internship journal her college wants to My Desk. Her advisor sent it back,
   and she asks me for regular meetings to go over what happens at the office. She has not looked me in the eye
   since the night of her text, and she has no idea I watched it.
   Part 2: Internship Overview Meetings 2, the first meeting, which advances the quest and unlocks the task. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[14].img>><</silent>>
For two days $sister.callName has been carrying a blue notebook around the office as if it holds the launch codes. She writes in it at her desk with one arm curled around the page, the way people guard a test from the guy next to them, and whenever I walk past she closes it on her pen.

She also hasn't looked me straight in the eye since the night she sent me that text. I'm fairly sure I know why, and she has no idea that I do.

Today the notebook comes to my desk. She sets it down next to my keyboard and then doesn't let go of it, so for a moment we're both just looking at her hand.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "I need a favor. It's a boring one, so you're not allowed to turn it down just for being boring." },
{ who: $player, text: "That rules out my favorite excuse, but go on." },
{ who: $sister, text: "My college wants an internship journal, one entry a week on what I did, what I learned and how it connects to the company's processes. I have been writing it, in my defense. You'll see the problem." },
{ text: "She flips the notebook open to the first page and turns it toward me." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Read it">>
The handwriting is neat, round and very determined.

<i>Monday. Brought coffee. Organized the supply cabinet by color.</i>
<i>Tuesday. Brought coffee. The good stapler is NOT in the supply cabinet. Investigating.</i>
<i>Wednesday. Brought coffee, but better. Learned that the coffee machine has a descaling button.</i>

Under Wednesday somebody has written in red pen, in the small, tired hand of a person who grades a lot of these: <i>Please reflect on the company's processes.</i>

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "In fairness, nobody has ever told me what the company's processes are. I know where the good stapler isn't, and that's roughly the extent of my institutional knowledge." },
{ who: $player, text: "So you want me to give you some processes." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I want meetings. Real ones, in the calendar. Every couple of days you tell me what's going on around here, the clients, the projects, whatever I'm allowed to know, and I write it down so it sounds like I understood it. An internship overview." },
{ text: "She says 'internship overview' very carefully, like a phrase she found online and practiced in the bathroom mirror." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Twenty minutes, tops, and I'll bring the coffee. You'll barely notice I'm there." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She could get every bit of that from $mom.callName, who keeps the calendar and knows every client down to the names of their kids, and she must know that as well as I do. She came to my desk anyway. What she's really asking for is a room with a door, every couple of days, booked under her name.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Why wait? Grab your journal and we'll do the first one right now, in the meeting room." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Right now? I haven't even made the coffee yet, and the coffee was my whole pitch." },
{ who: $player, text: "I think I'll survive one meeting without it. Bring the journal, and a pen that works." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

[[Go to the meeting room|Internship Overview Meetings 2]]
<</linkreplace>>
